<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William II, Elector of Hesse</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1777">1777</a>–<a href="/years/1847">1847</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William II, Elector of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, ruled the Electorate of Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassel">Kassel</a> from 1821. His autocratic rule and quarrels with his family provoked unrest, and after the revolution of 1830 he accepted a constitution and left government to his son Frederick William as co-regent. He spent his last years away from Kassel and died in 1847.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-ii-elector-of-hesse.jpg" alt="William II, Elector of Hesse" width="201" height="247" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Conrad Bodenstein · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_II,_elector_of_hesse.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
